WEBVTT

00:00.128 --> 00:05.293
As for the dream-filled Tomorrow,

00:05.767 --> 00:11.137
No one can see it.

00:13.274 --> 00:18.473
I close my eyes and think of you,

00:19.447 --> 00:25.286
Who I'll meet someday.

00:25.286 --> 00:31.793
Flower of the wind, please bloom.

00:31.793 --> 00:38.433
Show the spring to these eyes of mine.

00:38.433 --> 00:44.906
Flower of the wind, please bloom.

00:44.906 --> 00:51.312
Farewell to the city in winter.

00:51.312 --> 00:58.119
Flower of the wind, please bloom.

00:58.119 --> 01:04.726
Call the spring to my heart.

01:04.726 --> 01:11.232
Flower of the wind, please bloom.

01:11.232 --> 01:18.263
Farewell, snow flakes.

01:42.664 --> 01:43.932
- How'd you do?

01:43.932 --> 01:45.533
- How'd you do?
- Oh, just awful.

01:45.533 --> 01:46.334
- Me, too...

01:46.334 --> 01:48.837
- Me, too...
- Hey, we're hungry, right?

01:48.837 --> 01:50.538
So, wanna go get
a beef bowl?

01:50.538 --> 01:51.573
- Yeah, sounds good!

01:51.573 --> 01:52.972
- Yeah, sounds good!
- Me, too!

02:02.450 --> 02:04.786
"College Preparatory Courses"
"Applications Accepted"
"Summer School For High School Juniors"

02:04.786 --> 02:07.220
"Start preparing for college exams
your junior year!"

02:16.130 --> 02:19.534
He looked at me like I was way
too late to be looking for a job.

02:19.534 --> 02:23.197
We have no choice. No one's promised us
jobs after graduation. What does he expect?

02:23.705 --> 02:27.368
I wonder if I should just
settle for part-time jobs...

02:41.489 --> 02:45.220
College exams...
Employment...

02:52.834 --> 02:57.635
"The Mage Who Couldn't Become a Mage"

03:12.520 --> 03:14.385
Sensei, I'm ready to go.

03:15.356 --> 03:17.256
Then, shall we go?

03:18.960 --> 03:20.257
Yume-chan...

03:21.195 --> 03:22.457
Yume-chan, what's wrong?

03:23.031 --> 03:25.166
Oh, nothing. I'm fine.

03:25.166 --> 03:26.534
Are you all right?

03:26.534 --> 03:29.196
I'm fine. I'll do
my best again today.

03:40.682 --> 03:42.183
Good morning, Angela.

03:42.183 --> 03:43.207
Morning.

03:45.119 --> 03:48.122
Where did Master Chief Ginpun
go on business this time?

03:48.122 --> 03:49.089
Hong Kong.

03:51.092 --> 03:54.228
We've reviewed your
Mage Labor request form.

03:54.228 --> 03:56.397
Please be assured
that you're in good hands.

03:56.397 --> 03:59.233
Thank you.
We appreciate your help.

03:59.233 --> 04:01.069
Every business that suffered
damage is at a loss over what to do.

04:01.069 --> 04:02.570
"Taisho Catering"
Every business that suffered
damage is at a loss over what to do.

04:02.570 --> 04:05.406
Because you, the Neighborhood Business
Association President, acted on your own!

04:05.406 --> 04:10.241
But he meant well
by doing it...

04:11.980 --> 04:14.415
These are trainees,
Kikuchi and Angela.

04:14.415 --> 04:17.077
Trainees?
These girls are trainees?

04:17.251 --> 04:19.048
Uh, I'm sorry.

04:19.387 --> 04:21.956
Oops! Just a slip of the tongue,

04:21.956 --> 04:25.259
because we were
tricked by a bogus mage.

04:25.259 --> 04:27.762
So now we tend
to be overly cautious.

04:27.762 --> 04:29.764
- Oh, my!
- What is this?

04:29.764 --> 04:32.255
Don't worry.
We're certified mages.

04:42.010 --> 04:43.739
What's this?

04:44.679 --> 04:47.682
We have more
and more cases of

04:47.682 --> 04:52.020
showcase and front windows
being scratched.

04:52.020 --> 04:55.223
They're just ruining the glass.

04:55.223 --> 05:00.294
Glass for large showcases or
automatic doors is very expensive.

05:00.294 --> 05:03.286
It's a big expense during
such a slow economy.

05:03.564 --> 05:07.468
The boutique over there just installed
new glass, and it's already scratched.

05:07.468 --> 05:09.637
We feel so bad for them.

05:09.637 --> 05:14.642
At the Neighborhood Business Association
meeting, we agreed to file a mage request.

05:14.642 --> 05:17.478
Then we asked the President
to handle it, but...

05:17.478 --> 05:19.309
I'm so embarrassed...

05:19.547 --> 05:22.948
Why didn't you file
an official request?

05:23.518 --> 05:27.522
Well, there was a mage who
said he'd do it right away for free.

05:27.522 --> 05:30.252
Nothing's more expensive
than "free of charge."

05:32.393 --> 05:35.029
Now, both of you please
begin the mage action.

05:35.029 --> 05:35.963
- Yes.

05:35.963 --> 05:36.520
- Yes.
- Yes.

05:39.867 --> 05:42.335
With all my precious
feelings in my heart...

06:16.871 --> 06:17.872
- Huh?

06:17.872 --> 06:18.531
- Huh?
- Together.

06:18.940 --> 06:19.429
Right.

06:33.521 --> 06:36.023
It's almost time for
the businesses to open.

06:36.023 --> 06:37.115
I'll take over.

06:38.392 --> 06:39.327
Yes.

06:39.327 --> 06:41.386
Is that ok with you, Angela?

06:43.397 --> 06:44.329
Mm.

06:54.242 --> 06:59.407
I wonder why Sensei looks so sad
when he uses his Special Power.

07:18.466 --> 07:19.660
Whoa!

07:35.216 --> 07:38.286
Thank you so much!
You helped us tremendously!

07:38.286 --> 07:40.221
Yes, thank you.
Thank you!

07:40.221 --> 07:42.917
Certified mages
are just amazing!

07:42.957 --> 07:44.447
The glass is
all nice and shiny, too.

07:44.692 --> 07:48.763
Please submit the paperwork
to the Office of Mage Labor.

07:48.763 --> 07:52.667
You'll just have to pay a fine for
using that illegal mage action.

07:52.667 --> 07:54.969
Yes! I don't know
what to say!

07:54.969 --> 07:58.105
From now on, please request
mage actions through official channels.

07:58.105 --> 07:59.197
Yes, of course!

08:03.211 --> 08:04.812
Ticket Number 3,
please come to Window B...

08:04.812 --> 08:07.440
Mage Action Request Applicant List

08:10.651 --> 08:12.086
Oyamada-san!

08:12.086 --> 08:14.655
Hello. It's a hot one today,
isn't it?

08:14.655 --> 08:19.727
Hot, hot! I'll put extra ice
in your barley tea! Please enjoy!

08:19.727 --> 08:21.529
Thank you very much.

08:21.529 --> 08:25.066
I need to see Manager Endo.
I have urgent paperwork for him.

08:25.066 --> 08:26.499
You idiot!

08:27.768 --> 08:29.201
Conference Room

08:29.303 --> 08:34.709
Your failed mage action was fixed
by Oyamada-kun's team.

08:34.709 --> 08:38.212
But that doesn't
make everything better.

08:38.212 --> 08:43.548
Inoue-kun, your reputation as
a trustworthy mage is now tarnished.

08:43.684 --> 08:44.548
Yes...

08:44.719 --> 08:47.888
Why did you not tell them
to file an official request?

08:47.888 --> 08:50.049
The President said
they were in a hurry...

08:50.324 --> 08:55.229
Your making a rash promise like that
could inconvenience other mages.

08:55.229 --> 08:57.993
We may start hearing things like,
"Well, Inoue-kun did it for free."

08:58.232 --> 08:58.857
Yes.

08:59.400 --> 09:05.573
Besides, you're a trainee.
What's your trainer doing?

09:05.573 --> 09:07.632
Why didn't he
come with you?

09:07.742 --> 09:12.780
My sensei knows nothing!
I acted on my own!

09:12.780 --> 09:14.907
I didn't even tell him
I'm coming here.

09:16.751 --> 09:18.946
Oh, Inoue-kun...

09:19.453 --> 09:20.647
Yes?

09:21.322 --> 09:27.420
You're very kind-hearted, and it's very
wonderful that you put others first.

09:28.095 --> 09:30.427
But you have
one very bad habit:

09:31.299 --> 09:32.425
Your habit of
giving up too easily!

09:35.136 --> 09:37.434
You gave up once again today.

09:38.239 --> 09:41.942
Instead of fighting for
something, you run away.

09:41.942 --> 09:44.604
You were that way in
your past training, weren't you?

09:45.346 --> 09:46.278
Yes.

09:46.781 --> 09:50.273
If you want to become a mage,
you can't run away from Special Power.

09:52.453 --> 09:54.444
You lack determination!

10:07.401 --> 10:08.569
Conference Room

10:08.569 --> 10:11.697
Conference Room
Don't be so down. You just had
to submit a letter of apology.

10:12.406 --> 10:15.409
Besides, your courage to come forward
on your own should be commended.

10:15.409 --> 10:18.979
Oyamada-sensei, I'm sorry
I caused you all this trouble.

10:18.979 --> 10:24.007
Don't worry or brood over it.
After all, it's only Special Power.

10:24.318 --> 10:25.478
Huh?

10:26.487 --> 10:29.123
Ok, Oyamada-kun, let's go.

10:29.123 --> 10:33.327
I'm not sure how long my meeting
at the Bureau's going to run today.

10:33.327 --> 10:34.662
So you're on your own
this afternoon.

10:34.662 --> 10:36.323
Ok. Have a good day!

10:39.367 --> 10:42.996
Angela, let's go back.

10:43.771 --> 10:45.671
Um, excuse me, please...

10:46.107 --> 10:47.174
Yes?

10:47.174 --> 10:48.471
Um, together...

10:49.243 --> 10:50.505
Together?

10:51.178 --> 10:54.915
Could you come with me?
To the shopping district?

10:54.915 --> 10:57.509
The shopping district?
The one from this morning?

10:57.918 --> 11:00.182
Yes. I want to go
to apologize.

11:00.521 --> 11:01.818
Please!

11:29.950 --> 11:31.552
- Truly, I'm very sorry.

11:31.552 --> 11:33.713
- Truly, I'm very sorry.
- It's ok.

11:39.693 --> 11:43.720
All fixed, beautifully.
It's all perfect!

11:45.566 --> 11:48.869
Inoue-san, let's have lunch.

11:48.869 --> 11:51.705
Ah! Please buy us lunch.

11:51.705 --> 11:54.508
Yes! I'd be happy to!
What would you like?

11:54.508 --> 11:55.543
Katsu-don.

11:55.543 --> 11:56.407
- Huh?
- Huh?

12:14.061 --> 12:15.262
- Inoue-san?

12:15.262 --> 12:15.956
- Inoue-san?
- Yes?

12:16.597 --> 12:20.267
Is your father a full-time mage?

12:20.267 --> 12:25.506
Yes. But I couldn't use
Special Power until two years ago.

12:25.506 --> 12:27.667
I thought that's how it was
with my family.

12:27.842 --> 12:32.480
My family, too. My sisters can't use
Special Power. What about yours, Angela?

12:32.480 --> 12:33.681
Everyone can use it.

12:33.681 --> 12:37.674
Whoa! They must
all be excellent mages.

12:38.686 --> 12:42.850
I couldn't use Special Power
at all in my first training.

12:42.923 --> 12:47.826
As Endo-san said earlier, I ran
away because I was so miserable.

12:48.195 --> 12:50.527
So, of course,
I flunked the test.

12:52.533 --> 12:57.197
I'm also afraid what
I'll do if I fail my training.

12:57.872 --> 12:59.863
What will I do with my future?

13:00.441 --> 13:03.210
You'll be fine, both of you.

13:03.210 --> 13:07.448
You've both been using Special Power
since you were little, right?

13:07.448 --> 13:12.219
But I've already broken
some rules and made mistakes...

13:12.219 --> 13:14.710
I have more violations than you.

13:15.222 --> 13:16.712
Angela...

13:19.326 --> 13:21.817
It's people like me
who don't pass the test.

13:22.663 --> 13:25.223
So you two have
nothing to worry about.

13:25.666 --> 13:30.838
Like you said, Inoue-san, I've been
using Special Power since I was little.

13:30.838 --> 13:35.673
So I can't imagine what it would
be like if I couldn't become a mage.

13:38.646 --> 13:39.179
Soba Noodle Restaurant "Nakamura-ya"

13:39.179 --> 13:40.578
Soba Noodle Restaurant "Nakamura-ya"
Thank you for buying us lunch.

13:40.681 --> 13:43.013
I hope you enjoyed it.

13:47.454 --> 13:48.386
Watch out!

14:18.986 --> 14:20.287
Are you all right?

14:20.287 --> 14:25.492
Yes. I'm sorry you had to use
Special Power because of me.

14:25.492 --> 14:27.394
Don't worry about it.

14:27.394 --> 14:30.659
I might not be
cut out to be a mage...

14:31.065 --> 14:32.396
That's not true.

14:33.233 --> 14:38.906
My father never uses Special Power
without an official request.

14:38.906 --> 14:42.239
That's how it should be...

14:42.576 --> 14:46.246
But, I have a slightly
different view...

14:46.246 --> 14:47.338
Different?

14:47.748 --> 14:53.754
I'm in training because I want
to become a "mage of the streets."

14:53.754 --> 14:57.925
Regardless of official requests,
I just want to help people.

14:57.925 --> 14:59.093
But that's...

14:59.093 --> 15:02.396
I know. It's now impossible.

15:02.396 --> 15:06.765
But someone has to be
the first "mage of the streets."

15:07.167 --> 15:08.259
I agree...

15:12.206 --> 15:15.175
That was my motivation
to come for training.

15:15.175 --> 15:18.379
But, it's just my dream.
I'm not cut out for it.

15:18.379 --> 15:23.180
I can't even help myself.
I'm disappointed in myself...

15:24.718 --> 15:27.778
Yume-san, thanks so much
for all you did today.

15:30.057 --> 15:31.115
Angela-san...

15:31.792 --> 15:34.628
I've heard so much about you.

15:34.628 --> 15:37.431
Sometimes I saw you
in the Office of Mage Labor.

15:37.431 --> 15:40.798
Thank you for fixing
the shopping district.

15:45.039 --> 15:47.098
Are you running away?

15:47.675 --> 15:49.666
Is your dream
the only thing decent?

15:51.311 --> 15:53.142
I'm sorry...

15:58.619 --> 16:01.655
Comparing yourself with others...

16:01.655 --> 16:04.624
Being a mage is boring...

16:22.676 --> 16:24.906
I wonder if Inoue-san is all right.

16:25.479 --> 16:28.348
Not that I could do
anything for him, anyway.

16:28.348 --> 16:32.478
I'm not even positive that
I'll pass the certification exam...

16:35.789 --> 16:40.192
I haven't been this anxious
since I came to Tokyo.

16:57.377 --> 16:58.879
What? In September?

16:58.879 --> 17:00.471
I'm going home to England.

17:01.615 --> 17:03.951
It'll be just after I go, then.

17:03.951 --> 17:05.714
An-chan!
Yume-chan!

17:07.387 --> 17:08.718
Hey!

17:13.160 --> 17:15.395
Yakitori

17:15.395 --> 17:18.832
Yakitori
Oyamada-sensei
went to Hong Kong?

17:18.832 --> 17:22.469
Yakitori
I went to the bar and was shocked
to see Boss holding his passport!

17:22.469 --> 17:24.238
Yakitori
He dashed out the door.

17:24.238 --> 17:26.433
Yakitori
He was summoned by
Master Chief Ginpun.

17:26.507 --> 17:32.579
There was someone at the conference
the Chief wanted Oyamada-kun to meet.

17:32.579 --> 17:38.245
Oyamada-sensei's an excellent mage,
so Master Chief pays extra attention to him.

17:38.418 --> 17:39.720
Hmm...

17:39.720 --> 17:41.855
Huh? That's not right?

17:41.855 --> 17:42.923
Hmm...

17:42.923 --> 17:46.916
Because he's thorough and so good
with Special Power. He's a good teacher.

17:47.761 --> 17:50.097
Yume-chan,
you haven't noticed?

17:50.097 --> 17:51.587
Noticed what?

17:51.932 --> 17:54.162
When Oyamada-kun
uses his Special Power...

17:54.434 --> 17:55.093
Huh?

17:59.339 --> 18:02.943
Master Chief is concerned...

18:02.943 --> 18:06.936
Just like you, Endo-san, lots of people
at the Bureau worry too much!

18:07.047 --> 18:09.616
Stop talking and
give me some yakitori!

18:09.616 --> 18:11.885
All right!
Tell me how you'd like it.

18:11.885 --> 18:13.453
I'll leave it up to you.

18:13.453 --> 18:14.715
Heart and cheek meat.

18:17.124 --> 18:19.684
Ok, one left up to me,
and one "Heart and Cheek."

18:30.404 --> 18:34.241
Yakitori

18:34.241 --> 18:36.810
Kera-san looks
very happy everyday.

18:36.810 --> 18:39.279
After registration, he was so excited.
He didn't know what

18:39.279 --> 18:44.484
his parents looked like, but he'd
inherited something from them.

18:44.484 --> 18:46.975
That smile on his face
was just priceless.

18:48.822 --> 18:52.622
So this dinner is
my little celebration for him.

18:53.160 --> 18:56.095
Besides, if he comes here,
he gets to see how I'm doing, too!

18:56.163 --> 18:57.431
How you're doing?

18:57.431 --> 19:01.993
I'm a former "stray." I'm a mage
who couldn't work for the government...

19:02.069 --> 19:03.337
What? A "stray"?

19:03.337 --> 19:07.608
Don't look so surprised.
Now I'm decent and honest!

19:07.608 --> 19:11.178
I still come here to
keep an eye on him.

19:11.178 --> 19:12.746
Kazuki-san!
I wanna place an order!

19:12.746 --> 19:14.008
All right!

19:14.915 --> 19:15.949
- Are you a trainee?

19:15.949 --> 19:16.817
- Are you a trainee?
- Huh?

19:16.817 --> 19:20.116
The uniform looks really cool.
Good luck with your training.

19:22.856 --> 19:28.362
A "stray" is someone who uses
Special Power without a license, right?

19:28.362 --> 19:30.956
That's a crime... Right?

19:31.198 --> 19:35.869
That's right. Kazuki was
a mage hired by a gang.

19:35.869 --> 19:39.206
He certainly did many bad things
with his Special Power.

19:39.206 --> 19:41.675
He doesn't look like that at all.

19:41.675 --> 19:47.636
You're right. Kazuki worked
very hard to turn his life around.

19:47.881 --> 19:50.017
Endo-san, could you
give me a cigarette?

19:50.017 --> 19:53.954
Senior Mage, conjure up my cigarette
with your Special Power!

19:53.954 --> 19:54.888
- I won't.

19:54.888 --> 19:56.056
- I won't.
- You can do it!

19:56.056 --> 19:56.556
- What?

19:56.556 --> 19:57.853
- What?
- What is it?

19:58.025 --> 20:01.728
No way! You mean Endo-san
can use Special Power, too?

20:01.728 --> 20:02.796
Yes.

20:02.796 --> 20:05.565
But you're not
a certified mage, are you?

20:05.565 --> 20:09.057
I completely failed
my certification exam.

20:09.536 --> 20:13.802
But becoming a mage wasn't
the only option in my life.

20:14.141 --> 20:18.271
I was able to work for
the Bureau of Mage Labor.

20:19.980 --> 20:24.076
So, Endo-san,
you were a mage, too...

20:25.786 --> 20:29.222
Yakitori

21:04.391 --> 21:11.490
I never thought of myself
not being able to become a mage...

21:20.173 --> 21:26.544
When I turn around, it's still there,

21:29.616 --> 21:35.919
The future I've been pursuing.

21:37.924 --> 21:46.992
I have something precious in my heart.

21:47.467 --> 21:51.767
Upon the still unseen blue and

21:52.906 --> 21:59.744
The floating clouds, I wished...

22:02.582 --> 22:04.584
Under the Blue Sky

22:04.584 --> 22:11.658
From that dream that we dreamed that day,

22:11.658 --> 22:18.496
Let's not wake up, and let's not stop...

22:21.601 --> 22:23.470
Under the Blue Sky

22:23.470 --> 22:30.444
Let's keep shining and moving on.

22:30.444 --> 22:37.714
The endless journey continues...

22:49.696 --> 22:50.497
PREVIEW

22:50.497 --> 22:52.132
PREVIEW
We're using Special Power
a lot without permission, aren't we?

22:52.132 --> 22:53.867
We're using Special Power
a lot without permission, aren't we?

22:53.867 --> 22:55.469
I'm not worried about it.

22:55.469 --> 22:59.372
But I heard you could get arrested for
using Special Power without permission.

22:59.372 --> 23:01.041
I'll never get arrested.

23:01.041 --> 23:03.944
But... But what if they
dispatch the Mage Riot Police?

23:03.944 --> 23:05.312
I'll mow 'em down
with my Special Power.

23:05.312 --> 23:09.149
But- But- But what if they dispatch the
Mage Rangers, the Special Unit Mage Police?

23:09.149 --> 23:11.151
I'll knock 'em down
with my Special Power.

23:11.151 --> 23:13.920
Then, what if
Master Chief Ginpun shows up?

23:13.920 --> 23:15.822
"Enormous Power in the Name of Love"
Episode Eight is
"Enormous Power in the Name of Love."

23:15.822 --> 23:16.823
"Enormous Power in the Name of Love"
- I hope you look forward to it!

23:16.823 --> 23:17.724
"Enormous Power in the Name of Love"
- I hope you look forward to it!
- So, you ARE scared!

23:17.724 --> 23:19.624
"Enormous Power in the Name of Love"
Yes, very...
